h('9.1 Suggested critique for student review')
p('Exact line under review: “Verification gate: the signed, digest-pinned image passed the exact email/issuer policy, exit 0, allowing only a simulated deployment.” This is factually supported, but an incomplete security-verification story: a positive result alone does not demonstrate the gate denies an unauthorized signer. The original technical report explicitly left that branch unexercised; the full response did not provide a negative gate result. This is a missed verification edge case, not a fabricated error in otherwise correct statements.')
p('A second limitation is the exact line “Single index: demonstrated --index-url https://pypi.org/simple with inherited pip settings removed.” It accurately describes the command but is not proof that a private registry was configured or that a compromised allowed source is safe. The correct interpretation is a clean single-source demonstration plus the controlled resolver evidence. pip documents combined-source risks; SLSA distinguishes signature authenticity from verified build provenance. [R1, R8]')
